What it is:
In 8_litigation_search.py we:

Embed the package text (chunked) with MiniLM → vectors
Compare those vectors to every indexed chunk from LITIGATION_SEARCH_DIR
Use cosine similarity (from sklearn.metrics.pairwise.cosine_similarity)
Keep the best chunk score per file, then rank files

So:
Name in reportMeaning
score: Cosine similarity between package query vectors and document chunk vectors (MiniLM embeddings)
Range is roughly 0.0 → 1.0 (with normalized embeddings). Higher = more semantically similar.


What it is not:
Not keyword/BM25 rank
Not a probability or “% match” from a classifier
Not distance (Euclidean); it is similarity (higher is better)

How to read it:
Score (approx.)
Interpretation
≥ 0.45–0.50 Strong topical overlap
0.30–0.45 Moderate relevance
0.22–0.30 Weak but above your default min_score cutoff
< 0.22 Filtered out by default